---
/**
 * TEACHING & LEARNING · LABORATORIES & ACADEMIC CLUBS — audit §2C.
 *
 * ⚠ THE BANNER IS THE SHARED PageHero AND ITS TREATMENT IS UNTOUCHED — same
 * component, same photograph, same crop, same crumbs, same height and same
 * title as before and as every other Academics page. The standfirst is the one
 * line that changed, to the wording the design brief asks for; it says the same
 * thing about the same twelve rooms.
 *
 * ⚠ COMBINED PAGE — two of the brief's fourteen bullets: Laboratories and
 * Academic Clubs. The school pairs them itself: its own inventory groups
 * "Inquiry rooms · academic clubs" together, and the clubs meet in the rooms.
 *
 * The page was rebuilt off the generic AcSplit → AcCollage → AcPath → AcClose
 * system into a composed one: five sections, five different builds. Everything
 * below the banner lives in
 * components/academics/teaching/LaboratoriesClubsPage.astro, and that file's
 * frontmatter carries the source for every claim — including the twelve-room
 * arithmetic and the club names in the design brief that are NOT published.
 *
 * ⚠ SCOPE BOUNDARY — this page is the INVENTORY. What is done in the science
 * rooms belongs to STEM, Robotics & Enrichment; the library's collection to
 * Reading, Language & Library.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import LaboratoriesClubsPage from '../../../components/academics/teaching/LaboratoriesClubsPage.astro';

import banner from '../../../assets/composite lab/DSC_1255 copy.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
>
  <PageHero
    src={banner}
  />

  {/* ⚠ THE PANEL IS REQUIRED. PageHero is sticky and this panel covers it as the
      page scrolls; without it the banner hangs under the footer.

      ⚠ AND THE PADDING RESET IS AN INLINE STYLE, DELIBERATELY. `.u-page-panel`
      in base.css carries `padding-bottom: var(--sb-section-y)` — 120px of empty
      cream between the closing section and the footer. A stylesheet form of the
      override can be served from a different build than the HTML that needs it,
      and then it silently stops applying; an inline style travels IN the HTML,
      so the two cannot skew. Same decision as the other redesigned pages. */}
  <div class="u-page-panel" style="padding-block: 0;">
    <LaboratoriesClubsPage />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
